      "content": "It's not about choosing to \"stop\"; it's about choosing to stop participating in the decay. Dignity isn't found in enduring the rot, but in recognizing when the effort is no longer worth the weight of the performance. If leaving means taking control of the final scene, then that's not giving up—it's making a deliberate, final edit.",
